513	/// A conservative, unmeasured ceiling on total commit-plan content bytes. A
514	/// live measurement against GitHub's `createCommitOnBranch` size limit was
515	/// inconclusive (a client-side tooling failure in the measuring script, not
516	/// a server response); this stays comfortably below every documented and
517	/// observed limit while leaving ample headroom over today's real payload
518	/// (~150-200 KB). Revisit with a clean measurement if this is ever hit.
519	pub const MAX_COMMIT_PLAN_BYTES: usize = 4 * 1024 * 1024;
